OL,3,AFamily of prison officer killed by IRA
OL,4,Ato get state apology
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe family of a senior Irish prison
OL,7,Fofficer murdered by the IRA is to
OL,8,Freceive a state apology on Wednesday
OL,9,Ffor failings in investigations into his
OL,10,Fkilling.
OL,12,FBrian Stack, a father of three, was
OL,13,Fcrossing a street in Dublin, after
OL,14,Fleaving a boxing match in 1983, when he
OL,15,Fwas shot in the back of the neck.
OL,17,FStack, who was the chief prison officer
OL,18,Fat the high-security Portlaoise Prison,
OL,19,Fwas left paralysed and died 18 months
OL,20,Flater, aged 49.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
